{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Cap home heating oil prices to protect off-grid households from fuel poverty",
        "additional_details": "Unlike gas and electricity consumers who are safeguarded by the Ofgem price cap, many off-grid communities face severe financial hardship from unpredictable upfront costs. Heating a home is a basic necessity, and we feel it is unjust that rural or un-networked households are left completely vulnerable to market shocks. We urge the Government to regulate this sector and establish an equitable retail price cap.",
        "background": "Introduce statutory regulation and a fair price cap on domestic heating oil (kerosene) to shield off-grid consumers from extreme market volatility.\r\nOver 1.5 million UK homes rely on heating oil, leaving them exposed to sudden price spikes.",
